  "description": "One API over the Agora Voice SDK for Android and iOS: join a channel and publish/subscribe audio with awaitable calls and ordinary .NET events — plus the voice essentials (speakerphone routing, who-is-speaking volume reports, remote mute state, token renewal) — instead of writing a per-platform adapter over a Java event-handler class and an Objective-C delegate. Pulls in the platform binding that matches whichever target framework you build; the native artifacts carry no video codecs. Use Net.Agora.Video instead if the app ever shows or sends video. For .NET MAUI apps, add Net.Agora.Voice.Maui.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
